      "writtenOn": "2023-02-23T08:53:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for your reply. \n  Because the protection solution is customized for us, will use these vendor hooks, but the specific implementation details will be partly in vendor module and partly in the hypervisor, atf or other firmware. Also, each vendor\u0027s solution will be different. we don\u0027t want to open source,and I think other vendors will not want to share the details of their solution.\n  If we submit it to upstream, need to put all the details of the solution in kernel, including the vendor module. Now, we have two solution, one should trap into hypervisor and do the work, one is implemented in TEEOS, also the corresponding vendor modules are slightly different. It difficult to submit these vendor modules to upstream, and also will not be convenient for other vendor to customize.\n  How to do the documented? can you give me some advice. Thanks a lot!",
      "parentUuid": "7904f32d_43ed41b7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 52
